## Context

Track the staged implementation of backend design revision 5 as a contribution to 0725/#1333; preserve the website while migrating the existing evidence.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

Integration fixture: migrate one reported position and its evidence, keep another combination legacy, publish a candidate, then simulate a failed second edition. No duplicate ownership is allowed; the accepted site and earlier evidence chain must still replay.

## Actions

Coordinate 0761–0770 in the plan waves; reconcile the four country reports; hand accepted outputs to existing 0726–0728. Add the proposed research and release handoffs before those owners next execute. Do not close the programme tracker or start whole-transition/PyPSA work.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Every legacy table and row has a documented migration disposition
- [x] Four official-inventory migration reports are accepted with explicit unresolved coverage
- [x] Writer ownership and publication selection have no duplicate authority
- [x] Existing 0726–0728 acceptance includes two-edition replay and restoration with working routes/downloads
- [x] Research-critical history is retained; scientific and future-model work remains under its own owners

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

